# What this file is for
#
# The repo should contain the game source, the assets it needs, and the game's own
# design documents, and nothing else. Submission material (Devpost, videos, narration,
# thumbnails, the hackathon agent rules) lives in the sibling FarFromHome-Submission
# project. Everything below is either machine specific or easy to regenerate.
#
# Every rule here was checked with `git check-ignore -v` rather than assumed.

# Operating system and editor leftovers
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/

# Installed dependencies and secrets
node_modules/
.env
.env.local

# Build output
#
# dist/ holds the submission zip. Rebuild it any time with:
#   node build/package.js
dist/
*.zip
*.exe

# Local tool state
#
# Project skills under .claude/skills/ ARE tracked on purpose. They hold the code
# discovery rules and the design guardrails, and a fresh clone needs them. Only
# throwaway local state is ignored.
.claude/cache/
.claude/settings.local.json
.context/
.gemini/

# Python bytecode from tests/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scratch work
#
# One off scripts and debug captures. Not needed to build, play or judge the game.
scratch/
tools/
tests/screenshot_*.png
refactor.py
track-costs.js
tunnel_url.txt

# Reference images dropped loose into Docs/
#
# This only matches files directly inside Docs/, not subfolders, so the real
# screenshots in Docs/screenshots/ stay tracked. That is deliberate: they are
# referenced by the design documents.
Docs/*.jpg
Docs/*.jpeg
Docs/*.png
Docs/*.html
